    "# Experiment 2: State-of-the-Art (SOTA) Tools for Machine Learning Experiments & Project Development\n",
    "\n",
    "## Aim / Objective\n",
    "To conduct a comprehensive **State-of-the-Art (SOTA) Review** of tools, libraries, and frameworks utilized in modern Machine Learning (ML) experiments and software project development, accompanied by an empirical benchmark comparing data processing efficiency, model training speed across tree-based algorithms (`Scikit-Learn`, `XGBoost`, `LightGBM`), and a lightweight MLOps experiment tracking system.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## SOTA ML Tool Ecosystem & Taxonomy\n",
    "\n",
    "Modern machine learning engineering requires a specialized stack of tools across every phase of the project lifecycle:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n",
    "\u2502                      ML EXPERIMENTATION & DEVELOPMENT TAXONOMY              \u2502\n",
    "\u251c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2524\n",
    "\u2502 1. Data Engineering   : NumPy, Pandas, Polars, Dask                         \u2502\n",
    "\u2502 2. Data Visualization : Matplotlib, Seaborn, Plotly                         \u2502\n",
    "\u2502 3. Machine Learning   : Scikit-Learn, XGBoost, LightGBM, CatBoost           \u2502\n",
    "\u2502 4. Deep Learning      : PyTorch, TensorFlow, Keras                          \u2502\n",
    "\u2502 5. Model Interpretability: SHAP, LIME, Yellowbrick                          \u2502\n",
    "\u2502 6. MLOps & Tracking   : MLflow, Weights & Biases (W&B), DVC, Hydra          \u2502\n",
    "\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### 1. Data Engineering & Array Computation\n",
    "- **NumPy**: De facto matrix and multi-dimensional array computation engine in Python. Provides C-optimized vectorized operations.\n",
    "- **Pandas**: High-level data manipulation library providing DataFrames, data cleaning, tabular indexing, and file I/O.\n",
    "- **Polars**: Modern Rust-backed DataFrame library optimized for multi-threading and lazy evaluation on massive datasets.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### 2. Exploratory Data Analysis & Visualization\n",
    "- **Matplotlib**: Core low-level charting engine for publication-quality static graphics.\n",
    "- **Seaborn**: High-level statistical visualization layer built on Matplotlib offering clean aesthetic presets.\n",
    "- **Plotly**: Dynamic, web-interactive JavaScript-backed graphing library.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3. Machine Learning & Gradient Boosted Decision Trees (GBDT)\n",
    "- **Scikit-Learn**: Industry standard toolkit for classical supervised/unsupervised algorithms, data preprocessing, scaling, cross-validation, and metrics.\n",
    "- **XGBoost (eXtreme Gradient Boosting)**: Scalable, highly accurate GBDT library utilizing regularized objective functions and exact/approximate greedy tree splits.\n",
    "- **LightGBM**: Fast, distributed gradient boosting framework developed by Microsoft utilizing Gradient-based One-Side Sampling (GOSS) and Exclusive Feature Bundling (EFB).\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### 4. Deep Learning & Neural Frameworks\n",
    "- **PyTorch**: Preferred framework for AI research and modern production, featuring dynamic computation graphs (Eager execution) and automatic differentiation (`autograd`).\n",
    "- **TensorFlow**: Enterprise production deep learning ecosystem with static graph optimization and deployment tools (`TFLite`, `TF Serving`).\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### 5. MLOps, Versioning & Experiment Tracking\n",
    "- **MLflow**: Open-source platform for logging parameters, metrics, code versions, and deploying model artifacts.\n",
    "- **Weights & Biases (W&B)**: Enterprise MLOps platform for real-time loss tracking, hyperparameter sweeps, and model lineage.\n",
    "- **DVC (Data Version Control)**: Git-like version control system for large datasets and model weights."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 1. Load core diagnostic and benchmark libraries\n",
    "import os\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "import time\n",
    "import datetime\n",
    "import platform\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "from sklearn.datasets import load_breast_cancer\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "from sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score, precision_score, recall_score, f1_score, roc_auc_score\n",
    "\n",
    "import xgboost as xgb\n",
    "import lightgbm as lgb\n",
    "\n",
    "SEED = 42\n",
    "np.random.seed(SEED)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.style.use('seaborn-v0_8-whitegrid' if 'seaborn-v0_8-whitegrid' in plt.style.available else 'default')\n",
    "sns.set_theme(style=\"whitegrid\")\n",
    "%matplotlib inline\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Libraries loaded successfully.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. System & ML Library Diagnostic Audit"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 2. Perform automated tool inspection and version audit\n",
    "print(f\"OS Platform     : {platform.system()} {platform.release()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Python Version   : {sys.version.split()[0]}\")\n",
    "print(\"-\" * 60)\n",
    "\n",
    "tools = [\n",
    "    (\"Data Processing\", \"numpy\", \"NumPy\"),\n",
    "    (\"Data Processing\", \"pandas\", \"Pandas\"),\n",
    "    (\"Scientific Compute\", \"scipy\", \"SciPy\"),\n",
    "    (\"Visualization\", \"matplotlib\", \"Matplotlib\"),\n",
    "    (\"Visualization\", \"seaborn\", \"Seaborn\"),\n",
    "    (\"Classical ML\", \"sklearn\", \"Scikit-Learn\"),\n",
    "    (\"Gradient Boosting\", \"xgboost\", \"XGBoost\"),\n",
    "    (\"Gradient Boosting\", \"lightgbm\", \"LightGBM\"),\n",
    "    (\"Deep Learning\", \"torch\", \"PyTorch\"),\n",
    "    (\"Statistical Modeling\", \"statsmodels\", \"Statsmodels\")\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "audit_res = []\n",
    "for cat, mod_name, disp_name in tools:\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        m = __import__(mod_name)\n",
    "        v = getattr(m, \"__version__\", \"Available\")\n",
    "        audit_res.append({\"Category\": cat, \"Tool\": disp_name, \"Status\": \"Installed\", \"Version\": v})\n",
    "    except ImportError:\n",
    "        audit_res.append({\"Category\": cat, \"Tool\": disp_name, \"Status\": \"Not Installed\", \"Version\": \"N/A\"})\n",
    "\n",
    "df_audit = pd.DataFrame(audit_res)\n",
    "display(df_audit.style.highlight_max(subset=['Status'], color='lightgreen'))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. High-Performance Data Processing Benchmark (NumPy vs Pandas)\n",
    "\n",
    "Evaluating execution time on 1,000,000 array elements for mathematical transformations."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 3. Benchmark NumPy vs Pandas vectorized operations\n",
    "n_samples = 1_000_000\n",
    "data_arr = np.random.randn(n_samples)\n",
    "data_ser = pd.Series(data_arr)\n",
    "\n",
    "# NumPy vectorized benchmark\n",
    "t0 = time.perf_counter()\n",
    "res_np = np.sin(data_arr) ** 2 + np.cos(data_arr) ** 2\n",
    "t_np = (time.perf_counter() - t0) * 1000  # ms\n",
    "\n",
    "# Pandas vectorized benchmark\n",
    "t0 = time.perf_counter()\n",
    "res_pd = np.sin(data_ser) ** 2 + np.cos(data_ser) ** 2\n",
    "t_pd = (time.perf_counter() - t0) * 1000  # ms\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"NumPy Array Vectorized Computation  : {t_np:.3f} ms\")\n",
    "print(f\"Pandas Series Vectorized Computation: {t_pd:.3f} ms\")\n",
    "print(f\"NumPy Acceleration Factor          : {t_pd / t_np:.2f}x faster\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot speed comparison\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(7, 4))\n",
    "bars = plt.bar(['NumPy (Raw Arrays)', 'Pandas (Series DataFrames)'], [t_np, t_pd], color=['#1f77b4', '#ff7f0e'], width=0.45)\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Execution Time (ms)', fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.title('Data Processing Runtime: 1M Trigonometric Operations', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "for bar in bars:\n",
    "    plt.annotate(f'{bar.get_height():.2f} ms', xy=(bar.get_x() + bar.get_width()/2, bar.get_height()),\n",
    "                 xytext=(0, 3), textcoords=\"offset points\", ha='center', va='bottom', fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Modeling & GBDT Tooling Benchmark (`Scikit-Learn` vs `XGBoost` vs `LightGBM`)\n",
    "\n",
    "Benchmarking training speed, accuracy, and F1-scores on Breast Cancer Wisconsin dataset."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 4. Define Lightweight MLOps Experiment Tracker\n",
    "class LightweightExperimentTracker:\n",
    "    def __init__(self, experiment_name=\"SOTA_Tooling_Benchmark\"):\n",
    "        self.experiment_name = experiment_name\n",
    "        self.runs = []\n",
    "        \n",
    "    def log_run(self, run_name, model_name, runtime_ms, metrics):\n",
    "        self.runs.append({\n",
    "            \"Run ID\": f\"run_{len(self.runs)+1:03d}\",\n",
    "            \"Model / Framework\": model_name,\n",
    "            \"Timestamp\": datetime.datetime.now().strftime(\"%H:%M:%S\"),\n",
    "            \"Training Runtime (ms)\": round(runtime_ms, 2),\n",
    "            **metrics\n",
    "        })\n",
    "        \n",
    "    def get_leaderboard(self):\n",
    "        return pd.DataFrame(self.runs)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Lightweight MLOps Tracker initialized.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 5. Train and Benchmark Classifiers\n",
    "cancer = load_breast_cancer(as_frame=True)\n",
    "X, y = cancer.data, cancer.target\n",
    "feature_names = cancer.feature_names\n",
    "\n",
    "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(X, y, test_size=0.2, random_state=SEED, stratify=y)\n",
    "\n",
    "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
    "X_train_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(X_train)\n",
    "X_test_scaled = scaler.transform(X_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "tracker = LightweightExperimentTracker()\n",
    "\n",
    "models = {\n",
    "    \"Scikit-Learn Random Forest\": RandomForestClassifier(n_estimators=100, max_depth=6, random_state=SEED),\n",
    "    \"XGBoost Classifier\": xgb.XGBClassifier(n_estimators=100, max_depth=4, learning_rate=0.1, random_state=SEED, eval_metric='logloss'),\n",
    "    \"LightGBM Classifier\": lgb.LGBMClassifier(n_estimators=100, max_depth=4, learning_rate=0.1, random_state=SEED, verbosity=-1)\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "importance_dict = {}\n",
    "\n",
    "for name, model in models.items():\n",
    "    start = time.perf_counter()\n",
    "    model.fit(X_train_scaled, y_train)\n",
    "    runtime = (time.perf_counter() - start) * 1000\n",
    "    \n",
    "    y_pred = model.predict(X_test_scaled)\n",
    "    y_prob = model.predict_proba(X_test_scaled)[:, 1]\n",
    "    \n",
    "    metrics = {\n",
    "        \"Accuracy\": accuracy_score(y_test, y_pred),\n",
    "        \"Precision\": precision_score(y_test, y_pred),\n",
    "        \"Recall\": recall_score(y_test, y_pred),\n",
    "        \"F1-Score\": f1_score(y_test, y_pred),\n",
    "        \"ROC-AUC\": roc_auc_score(y_test, y_prob)\n",
    "    }\n",
    "    \n",
    "    tracker.log_run(run_name=name, model_name=name, runtime_ms=runtime, metrics=metrics)\n",
    "    if hasattr(model, 'feature_importances_'):\n",
    "        importance_dict[name] = model.feature_importances_\n",
    "\n",
    "df_leaderboard = tracker.get_leaderboard()\n",
    "print(\"MLOps Experiment Tracker Leaderboard:\")\n",
    "display(df_leaderboard.style.highlight_max(subset=['Accuracy', 'F1-Score', 'ROC-AUC'], color='lightgreen').highlight_min(subset=['Training Runtime (ms)'], color='lightgreen'))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 6. Visualizing Model Runtimes and Performance Metrics\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 5))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Runtime comparison\n",
    "bars = axes[0].bar(df_leaderboard[\"Model / Framework\"], df_leaderboard[\"Training Runtime (ms)\"], color=['#1f77b4', '#2ca02c', '#d62728'], width=0.45)\n",
    "axes[0].set_title('Framework Training Runtime (ms)', fontweight='bold')\n",
    "axes[0].set_ylabel('Milliseconds')\n",
    "axes[0].tick_params(axis='x', rotation=15)\n",
    "for bar in bars:\n",
    "    axes[0].annotate(f'{bar.get_height():.1f} ms', xy=(bar.get_x() + bar.get_width()/2, bar.get_height()),\n",
    "                     xytext=(0, 3), textcoords=\"offset points\", ha='center', va='bottom', fontweight='bold')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Metrics comparison bar chart\n",
    "df_metrics_plot = df_leaderboard.set_index(\"Model / Framework\")[[\"Accuracy\", \"F1-Score\", \"ROC-AUC\"]].T\n",
    "df_metrics_plot.plot(kind='bar', ax=axes[1], width=0.75, colormap='tab10')\n",
    "axes[1].set_title('Classification Performance Metrics', fontweight='bold')\n",
    "axes[1].set_ylim(0.9, 1.01)\n",
    "axes[1].legend(loc='lower right')\n",
    "axes[1].tick_params(axis='x', rotation=0)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 7. Feature Importance Analysis across Tree Frameworks\n",
    "df_imp = pd.DataFrame(importance_dict, index=feature_names)\n",
    "df_imp[\"Mean Importance\"] = df_imp.mean(axis=1)\n",
    "top8_imp = df_imp.sort_values(by=\"Mean Importance\", ascending=False).head(8)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))\n",
    "top8_imp[list(importance_dict.keys())].plot(kind='barh', figsize=(10, 5))\n",
    "plt.title('Top 8 Feature Importance Scores Across SOTA Tree Frameworks', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Relative Feature Importance')\n",
    "plt.gca().invert_yaxis()\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
